<article class="env-lemma" id="0ASB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ASB">Lemma <span data-tag="0ASB">15.25.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. Let $M$ be a flat $A$-module. Let $x \in M$. The content ideal of $x$, if it exists, is finitely generated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Say $x \in IM$. Then we can write $x = \sum _{i = 1, \ldots , n} f_ i x_ i$ with $f_ i \in I$ and $x_ i \in M$. Hence $x \in I'M$ with $I' = (f_1, \ldots , f_ n)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>